      "message": "feat(cli): --skill <folder|claude|copilot> install writes an AI agent skill\n\n`camcraft-cli --skill <target> install [--dir <path>] [--user] [--force]`\nwrites a skill that teaches the CLI to an AI agent. The text has one\nsource: the body crates/app/src/cli_skill.md, then the CLI's own usage\ntexts (TOP_USAGE and each HELP_LANES entry), so the reference cannot\ndrift from the binary.\n\n- folder: <dir>/SKILL.md\n- claude: .claude/skills/camcraft-cli/SKILL.md (project; --user: home)\n- copilot: .github/instructions/camcraft-cli.instructions.md\n\nAn existing file is refused with exit 1 unless --force is given.\nDecisions in docs/decisions/3751-cli-skill-install.md.\n\nFixes #3751\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
